  "item": [
    {
      "id": "613a14b9-043d-455a-9e9a-3aa72c97defe",
      "name": "Assets",
      "description": {
        "content": "Assets encompass all the value that flows through the Flexa platform. In the Flexa API, both national currencies (“fiat“) and digital currencies (“crypto“ or “digital assets“) are returned together in one collection.\n\nThe Flexa API uses [CAIP](https://chainagnostic.org/CAIPs/caip-19)-style IDs for all assets. National currency asset IDs are all prefixed with “iso4217/” and use [ISO 4217](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_4217) 3-digit alphabetic codes. For example, ether on Ethereum mainnet is `eip155:1/slip44:60`, and the Canadian dollar is `iso4217/CAD`.\n",
        "type": "text/plain"
      },
